{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"69124710020becbfe690bc32ecbcba0ba21a3be732f457e8800e081562f14a06","digest":{"component_or_area":"CI/CD workflow (.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml)","key_entities":[".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml","golden-path job","jq","apt-get update","type jq >/dev/null 2>&1"],"problem_keywords":["redundant apt-get update","jq installation","github actions performance","ci workflow optimization"],"propositions":["The golden-path job in gerrit-verify.yaml unconditionally runs apt-get update on every run despite jq being pre-installed on ubuntu-latest runners, incurring 15-30s of redundant overhead.","A conditional check using `type jq` can detect the presence of jq in <0.001s and skip apt-get update when jq is already available.","The conditional fallback approach safely handles both standard runners with jq pre-installed and minimal environments lacking jq.","The merged change implements the conditional check in the golden-path job step and passes all acceptance criteria including lint, typecheck, and workflow parity tests."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787548795772642001,"uuid":"c7234e16-35ed-4af5-8f4b-2b4abefe176e"}